('41', '6', '2', '8', '\\documentclass{article}\r\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\r\n\r\n\\title{Laplacian Operator}\r\n\r\n\\begin{document}\r\n\r\n\\maketitle\r\n\r\nThe Laplacian operator \\(\\nabla^2\\) in Cartesian coordinates is:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\nabla^2 f(x, y, z) = \\frac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x^2} + \\frac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y^2} + \\frac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial z^2}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\n\\end{document}', NULL, NULL),
('42', '6', '2', '9', '\\documentclass{article}\r\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\r\n\r\n\\title{Gradient of a Scalar Field}\r\n\r\n\\begin{document}\r\n\r\n\\maketitle\r\n\r\nThe gradient of a scalar field \\(f(x, y, z)\\) is:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\nabla f = \\left( \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}, \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}, \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z} \\right)\r\n\\]\r\n\r\n\\end{document}', NULL, NULL),
('43', '6', '2', '10', '\\documentclass{article}\r\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\r\n\r\n\\title{Divergence of a Vector Field}\r\n\r\n\\begin{document}\r\n\r\n\\maketitle\r\n\r\nThe divergence of a vector field \\(\\mathbf{F} = (F_x, F_y, F_z)\\) is:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F} = \\frac{\\partial F_x}{\\partial x} + \\frac{\\partial F_y}{\\partial y} + \\frac{\\partial F_z}{\\partial z}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\n\\end{document}', NULL, NULL),
('44', '6', '2', '11', '\\documentclass{article}\r\n\\usepackage{amsmath}\r\n\r\n\\title{Curl of a Vector Field}\r\n\r\n\\begin{document}\r\n\r\n\\maketitle\r\n\r\nThe curl of a vector field \\(\\mathbf{F} = (F_x, F_y, F_z)\\) is:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F} = \\left( \\frac{\\partial F_z}{\\partial y} - \\frac{\\partial F_y}{\\partial z}, \\frac{\\partial F_x}{\\partial z} - \\frac{\\partial F_z}{\\partial x}, \\frac{\\partial F_y}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial F_x}{\\partial y} \\right)\r\n\\]\r\n\r\n\\end{document}', NULL, NULL),
